  "method": "Within every original-valid opening run, choose consecutive disjoint blocks of 601 rows. Mask the final 600 readings and hold the first reading constant as the only original anchor. Every horizon uses the same blocks. Errors summarize all masked positions up to that horizon.",
  "limitations": [
    "Artificially masked valid blocks do not establish actual sensor-fault reconstruction accuracy.",
    "This is a descriptive masking experiment, not a learned model or a held-out forecasting score.",
    "Rapid opening adjustments can make carry-forward estimates wrong even when the anchor is recent.",
    "The longest-window eligibility restriction excludes original-valid runs shorter than 601 observations.",
    "No source readings or published Silver tables are changed by this experiment."
